course: dictionary
lesson: 13215
title: Furthest: how far is far?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Furthest is the top step of the word far. Far means a long way away, further means more far, and furthest means the most far: the greatest distance of all. «Ali threw the ball the furthest.» Of the whole class, Ali's throw went the longest distance.
explain: Look for clues like the word the before furthest. «The furthest planet» means the one farthest from the Sun, not just any far planet. Farthest is another form you may see, and it means the same for distance.
explain: Furthest can also mean to the greatest degree or extent. «She had gone the furthest in her reading of anyone in the class» is about how much, not how many metres. Ask yourself: is it about distance, or about how much? Either way, furthest means the most.
fact: Furthest is the superlative of far: far, further, furthest.
fact: Farthest is another form that means the same thing for distance.
fact: «Furthest» means at the greatest distance, the most far away.
fact: «The furthest point» on a map is the one that is farthest from where you start.
fact: In a comparison, the furthest is the biggest distance, so find the longest of all the distances.
exercise: «Who threw the ball the furthest?» What does furthest mean in this sentence? | *The longest distance | The fewest throws | The most colourful ball | The loudest cheer
exercise: Ben ran 40 metres, Sara ran 55 metres and Tom ran 48 metres. Who ran the furthest? | *Sara | Tom | Ben | Everyone ran the same
exercise: Which word means the same as furthest when we talk about distance? | shortest | closest | *farthest | nearest
test: «The rocket flew the furthest of all the rockets.» What does furthest mean here? | *The greatest distance | The most colours | The longest wait | The smallest size
test: Maya walked 2 km, Ravi walked 3 km and Ellie walked 1 km. Who walked the furthest? | They all walked the same | Ellie | Maya | *Ravi
exam: «She has gone the furthest in her learning of anyone in the class.» What does furthest mean? | *To the greatest degree or extent | Without any help | At the closest distance | Very slowly
